                                "sense_id": "19f91206-28cf-3ca9-935d-59a0b8905ef5",
                                "text": "Help me away, dear Charmian, I shall fall:"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6c047f4-1a93-4c92-b979-ef4eb3bff04c",
                                "sense_id": "19f91206-28cf-3ca9-935d-59a0b8905ef5",
                                "text": "Charmian Lyle had given herself her first name at the age of sixteen, upon encountering it in an English novel. Her baptismal name was Ethel. When her husband Walter was extremely angry with her, he called her Ethel. Charmian, she thought, suited her much better. She didn't think she looked, felt, or sounded like Ethel. Nor like her middle name, which she really detested, Edna."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
